S11 is Return Loss. Equation: S11 = V_reflected / V_incident (at Port 1).
S21 is Insertion Loss. Equation: S21 = V_transmitted_to_Port_2 / V_incident_at_Port_1.

{{image_1}}

S22 is Output Return Loss. Equation: S22 = V_reflected / V_incident (at Port 2).
S12 is Reverse Isolation. Equation: S12 = V_transmitted_to_Port_1 / V_incident_at_Port_2.

{{image_1}}

1) Widening the trace: Increases Capacitance, Decreases Inductance, Decreases Resistance.
2) Lengthening the trace: Increases Capacitance, Increases Inductance, Increases Resistance.

{{image_1}}

1) Increase the spacing between traces (e.g., the "3W rule").
2) Route adjacent layers perpendicularly (orthogonal routing).
